block head
    title Anorectal Nerve Damage - Plants Cause Disease

block content
    h1 Anorectal Nerve Damage
    p Definition by #[a(href="https://www.mayoclinichealthsystem.org/locations/mankato/services-and-treatments/gastroenterology-and-hepatology/digestive-and-liver-disorders/fecal-incontinence") Mayo Clinic]:
    blockquote Injury to the nerves that sense stool in the rectum or those that control the anal sphincter can lead to fecal incontinence. The nerve damage can be caused by childbirth, constant straining during bowel movements, spinal cord injury or a stroke.